    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (71.91) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.41) serving as our primary engines. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Springs, where park factors and a high-upside SP matchup combine to outweigh the dynamic platoon penalty. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** is an elite start at catcher; his leadoff role provides a significant floor for Runs, and his ability to exploit a 4.74 xERA makes him our most efficient play. **Kyle Tucker** (70.18) remains a high-floor start despite a difficult matchup against Valdez, as his power-speed profile consistently defies SP-skill regression, making him a must-start in our ongoing pursuit of those scarce stolen bases.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon dynamics, most notably with **Coby Mayo** (66.72), who receives a significant boost against Springs due to favorable park factors and, surprisingly, a positive dynamic platoon adjustment that pushes his value well above his baseline projection. Conversely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.39) and **Jackson Merrill** (48.63) are operating near our efficiency threshold. **Jackson Merrill** is a notable risk today; while he benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Rasmussen, the low xERA of the opposing pitcher makes this a precarious start for your limited game caps. The most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (55.38), who was narrowly squeezed out of the starting nine. While **Miguel Vargas** boasts a strong xwOBA of .373 and a beneficial matchup against Matthews, the optimizer prioritized the higher-order stability and park-adjusted output of **Sam Antonacci** and **Tommy White**, leaving **Miguel Vargas** as the primary pivot should any late-inning substitutions arise. Keep a close eye on the weather and the final lineup cards, as any shifts in the batting order for **Nasim Nunez** or **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014the latter of whom is currently facing a very favorable 6.99 xERA matchup\u2014could meaningfully shift our daily production ceiling.",
